# Generated output — never 3-way-merge it (multi-agent-git-workflow rule §D1).
#
# `.claude/` is 42 files written by `lib/install-defaults.sh` from `commands/`,
# `defaults/` and `tools/`. It is committed (the harness loads it) AND generated,
# so it conflicts on every overlap even when the source does not — and it cannot
# be partitioned between sessions, because a change to any playbook rewrites it.
# In one afternoon ADT-264 rebased four times, every collision in this tree and
# none in the source it is generated from (#265, #267, #268, #270, #271).
#
# `merge=ours` stops git reconciling these paths. Whoever merges second keeps
# their tree and REGENERATES it: `bash lib/resync.sh`, which is authoritative
# because the source is. Use resync rather than calling install-defaults.sh
# in place directly: it is the same regeneration, and it also names the
# playbooks whose installed copy changed, so you know which commands a session
# already running has loaded a stale copy of (ADT-306). `tests/test_installed_copies_match_source.sh`
# is what proves the regeneration actually happened.
#
# The driver is registered per-clone and is NOT carried by this file:
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
# Scoped to exactly the generated globs, never authored source (§D1).
.claude/**                 merge=ours
.claude/.adt-manifest.json merge=ours
